title: Pycrograph
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Boulter
    given-names: Etienne
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6597-9086"
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheBrickalista/Pycrograph"
license: GPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
# doi: added once the first release is archived on Zenodo
abstract: >
  Pycrograph is a GPLv3 Python desktop application for building
  publication figures from fluorescence microscopy images. Raw files
  (MetaMorph TIFF/STK) are registered by reference and never modified;
  every display setting (per-channel window, gamma, colour lookup table,
  orientation) is re-applied at render time. Provenance follows
  PysternBlot: SHA-256 source verification, hash-chained operation log
  and integrity reports.
keywords:
  - microscopy
  - immunofluorescence
  - figure
  - provenance
  - PySide6
  - Python
